//? Title: Image Explanations: Local Fits and Exact Coalition Credit
//? Subtitle: Tensor LIME, fixed-baseline Shapley values and signed CNN relevance on noisy bars
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Given one image and a classifier score, assign signed contributions to image
regions while making the reference image and target explicit. LIME fits a local
linear surrogate to masked predictions; exact coalition attribution averages
marginal changes over every ordering of the patches. We begin with three patches
whose interaction can be checked by hand, then explicitly train tensor CNN and
dense classifiers on the original noisy-bar task. Batched native C++ explainers
retain actual masks or coalition scores, measure fit quality and efficiency
residuals, and compare signed maps with a model-specific relevance rule.
Baseline and score changes expose which question each explanation answers.
)

\toc

> Three patches: share the interaction and retain the negative contribution

Let three one-pixel patches be on or off, a,b,c in {0,1}. The score
v(a,b,c)=2a+3b+6ab−c has additive contributions two, three and minus one,
plus an interaction of six when a and b are both present. In a random ordering,
a arrives after b half the time, and b arrives after a half the time. Each
receives three interaction units, giving Shapley values [5,6,−1]. Their sum
is ten, exactly the full score minus the empty score in this small game.
A negative attribution is part of the answer and must not be discarded.

The program reads all eight actual coalition scores and dispatch counts from
the tensor kernel. LIME fits the same game near the full coalition; its
coefficients need not split the interaction equally or sum to ten.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/xai_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  namespace n=dm::nn;std::filesystem::create_directories("build");n::set_num_threads(2);
  const auto image=n::ones({1,1,3,1},n::DType::Float64);
  n::ImageScoreBatch predict=[](const n::Tensor& x){const auto z=n::reshape(x,{x.size(0),3});const auto a=n::select(z,1,0),b=n::select(z,1,1),c=n::select(z,1,2);return 2*a+3*b+6*a*b-c;};
  n::ImagePatchOptions o;o.patch_rows=1;o.patch_cols=3;o.batch_size=3;
  const auto shap=n::exact_image_shapley(image,predict,o);n::ImageLimeOptions l;l.patches=o;l.samples=800;
  const auto lime=n::lime_image(image,predict,l);const auto phi=shap.patch_values.to_vector<double>();
  std::print("| integer mask | a | b | c | actual score |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  const auto scores=shap.coalition_scores.to_vector<double>();for(std::size_t s=0;s<scores.size();++s)std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {:.0f} |\n",s,s&1,(s>>1)&1,(s>>2)&1,scores[s]);
  std::print("\nShapley: {}; base {:.0f}; full {:.0f}; sum {:.0f}; efficiency residual {:.3g}; evaluations {}; batches {}; marginal terms {}.\n",phi,shap.base_value,shap.full_value,n::sum(shap.patch_values).item(),shap.efficiency_residual,shap.work.evaluations,shap.work.predict_calls,shap.work.marginal_terms);
  std::print("LIME: {}; intercept {:.6f}; weighted in-sample R2 {:.6f}; surrogate full {:.6f}; actual full {:.0f}.\n",lime.patch_values.to_vector<double>(),lime.intercept,lime.r_squared,lime.fitted_full,lime.full_value);
  if(phi!=std::vector<double>{5,6,-1}||shap.efficiency_residual!=0)throw std::runtime_error("tiny interaction attribution failed");
  dm::graphics::Diagram g(64,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=3.4;box.height=1.5;box.font_size=24;
  for(int j=0;j<3;++j){box.fill=j==2?dm::graphics::RGB{254,202,202}:dm::graphics::RGB{187,247,208};g.node(std::to_string(j),{5.*j,0},std::format("patch {}\ncredit {:.0f}",char('a'+j),phi[j]),box);}
  box.width=5;box.fill={191,219,254};g.node("interaction",{2.5,3.5},"interaction 6ab\nthree units to each",box).edge("interaction","0").edge("interaction","1")
    .text({5,5.6},"Actual game: 2a + 3b + 6ab - c",27).text({5,-2},"Signed credit 5 + 6 - 1 = full 10 - empty 0",25).save_svg("build/xai_tiny.svg");
}
