> Explain two new bars with one fixed raw target score

We generate a new horizontal and vertical example at position five using
seed 99. Each explanation fixes its target to that model's predicted class
on the full image; removing patches never changes which target column is
queried. The grid is the original 4×4, baseline zero, and LIME uses 800
samples. Exact attribution evaluates 65,536 masks, while LIME evaluates 800.
Both dispatch batches of at most 256 images.

Here the shared target is a raw logit, allowing a comparison in the same
score units with the native stabilised z-plus relevance rule. That rule
uses the CNN's actual weights and max-pool winners; it seeds the full raw
logit, omits biases and negative connections in redistribution denominators,
and can lose relevance mass through zero paths and epsilon. It is model
specific, may be signed, and does not promise a sum equal to full-minus-baseline.
The original report compared probability perturbations with raw-score relevance;
the next experiment makes the probability change explicit instead.

Patch scores are divided uniformly among their spatial pixels before display,
so each expanded map sums to its patch total up to rounding. This bookkeeping
does not infer within-patch resolution. Repeating the full patch score at every
pixel, as the old display did, would multiply each patch contribution by its
area. Native correlation keeps negative entries. Constant maps give an undefined
NaN correlation, rather than a fabricated zero.

Each signed map uses a blue-white-red key, with white zero and its own symmetric
numeric limits. The input uses a black-white zero-to-one key. Square cells retain
the image aspect. Colour brightness across differently scaled panels is not a
quantitative comparison. Numeric score sums and signed Pearson correlations provide the
comparison. The first image row appears at the top.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/xai_cnn_horizontal.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  namespace n=dm::nn;namespace m=n::models;n::set_num_threads(2);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");std::filesystem::create_directories("figures");n::ParameterStore p(1);{n::NoGradGuard guard;(void)m::SmallImageCnn(p,n::zeros({1,12,12,1}));}p.load("build/xai_cnn.npz");
  n::BarImageOptions b;b.min_position=5;b.max_position=5;const auto data=n::make_bar_images(1,99,b);n::ImagePatchOptions o;n::ImageLimeOptions l;l.samples=800;l.patches=o;std::vector<std::string> query_summaries;std::optional<dm::graphics::Diagram> primary;
  std::print("| example | target | full logit | baseline logit | sum Shapley | efficiency residual | LIME R2 | fitted full | z-plus pixel sum | corr LIME,Shapley | corr z-plus,Shapley |\n| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(int i=0;i<2;++i){const auto x=n::take_rows(data.images,{i});std::int64_t target;{n::NoGradGuard guard;target=n::argmax(m::SmallImageCnn(p,x).logits,1).item<std::int64_t>();}
    n::ImageScoreBatch score=[&](const n::Tensor& batch){return n::select(m::SmallImageCnn(p,batch).logits,1,target);};
    const auto shap=n::exact_image_shapley(x,score,o);const auto lime=n::lime_image(x,score,l);const auto relevance=m::SmallImageCnnZPlus(p,x,{target});
    const auto sp=n::expand_image_attributions(shap.patch_values,12,12),lp=n::expand_image_attributions(lime.patch_values,12,12),rp=relevance.input_relevance;
    std::print("| {} | {} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} | {:.3g} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} |\n",i?"vertical":"horizontal",target,shap.full_value,shap.base_value,n::sum(shap.patch_values).item(),shap.efficiency_residual,lime.r_squared,lime.fitted_full,n::sum(rp).item(),n::attribution_correlation(lp,sp),n::attribution_correlation(rp,sp));
    if(std::abs(shap.efficiency_residual)>1e-8||std::abs(n::sum(sp).item()-n::sum(shap.patch_values).item())>1e-8)throw std::runtime_error("efficiency or pixel-area conservation failed");
    auto picture=n::diagram_image_maps(n::concat({x,rp,lp,sp},0),2,{"Input intensity","Stabilised z-plus","Local LIME","Exact patch Shapley"},{false,true,true,true});
    if(i){picture.save_svg("build/xai_cnn_vertical.svg");std::filesystem::copy_file("build/xai_cnn_vertical.svg","figures/xai_cnn_vertical.svg",std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);}else primary=std::move(picture);
    query_summaries.push_back(std::format("{} queries: Shapley {} images / {} batches / {} marginals; LIME {} images / {} batches.",i?"Vertical":"Horizontal",shap.work.evaluations,shap.work.predict_calls,shap.work.marginal_terms,lime.work.evaluations,lime.work.predict_calls));}
  primary->save_svg("build/xai_cnn_horizontal.svg");
  for(const auto& summary:query_summaries)std::print("\n{}\n",summary);
}
